\section*{Zariski–Lipman conjecture}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
A singular normal affine complex surface is claimed to have a globally free rank-two tangent sheaf, contradicting the characteristic-zero Lipman--Zariski assertion. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 048, 2026-09-23): The analytic seed is a negative-curve neighborhood whose gluing is modified without changing its normal bundle. Two vector fields are built with a nonvanishing determinant off the curve by simultaneous point corrections and global residue constraints; algebraization preserves the completed singularity and allows tangent freeness to descend.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 048, 2026-09-23): The normal integral affine complex surface has Der\_C(A) free of rank two but a nonregular maximal localization. Thus its tangent/derivation module is free while the variety is singular, directly refuting the stated implication.

\subsection{Formal verification}
Family 048 has no Lean scope page in this snapshot; no formalization of these manuscript results is listed.

This site has not executed the Lean files or checked their dependencies. These descriptions report the scope of the linked declarations, rather than a new verification of the proofs.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these results to an internal model. Its release notice cautions that results lacking full formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently assessed the proofs; a solved label records the scope of the reported claim.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item OpenAI, \emph{A singular normal affine surface with free tangent sheaf}, 2026-09-23; citation key \texttt{OAI:A-singular-normal-affine-surface-with-free-tangent-sheaf-September-23-2026}. \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/A-singular-normal-affine-surface-with-free-tangent-sheaf-September-23-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (GitHub)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/raw/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/A-singular-normal-affine-surface-with-free-tangent-sheaf-September-23-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (direct)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/A-singular-normal-affine-surface-with-free-tangent-sheaf-September-23-2026/README.md}{Manuscript page and citation}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/main/preprints/A-singular-normal-affine-surface-with-free-tangent-sheaf-September-23-2026/paper.pdf}{Latest version}.
\item \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/CONTENTS.md}{OpenAI catalogue entry}.
